se-Checklist.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1077, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:40\", \"token_count\": 704, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-67\\n\\n# Slack Thread: A11y Audit Superseded\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-24\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:52] Alice**: Hey team, after reviewing the scope of the a11y fixes needed for the custom preview, we've decided to fold the remaining work into the main redaction preview UI task.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:57] Diana**: That makes sense. Most of the issues are in the preview pane anyway.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 13:58] Evan**: So we're not doing a separate audit report?\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 14:04] Bob**: Got it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 14:05] Alice**: No, we'll just include the accessibility requirements as part of the Definition of Done for the redaction preview UI. It's cleaner than tracking them separately.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 14:06] Bob**: Works for me. I'll move the CSS focus work over to that branch.\\n\\n**[2026-08-24 14:08] Alice**: Folding the a11y audit into the preview UI overhaul — no separate track. Let's focus all our GUI energy on getting that across the line.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 67 slack thread a11y audit supersed channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 24 2026 08 24 13 52 alic hey team after review the scope of the a11y fix need for the custom preview we ve decid to fold the remain work into the main redact preview ui task 2026 08 24 13 57 diana that make sens most of the issu are in the preview pane anyway 2026 08 24 13 58 evan so we re not do a separ audit report 2026 08 24 14 04 bob got it 2026 08 24 14 05 alic no we ll just includ the access requir a part of the definit of done for the redact preview ui it s cleaner than track them separ 2026 08 24 14 06 bob work for me i ll move the cs focus work over to that branch 2026 08 24 14 08 alic fold the a11y audit into the preview ui overhaul no separ track let s focus all our gui energi on get that across the line\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8d681d88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-a11y-superseded.md\", \"id\": \"ad88350ed6f27c58\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24016218250485974, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07172631786408536, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6331792, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-a11y-superseded.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8d681d88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-a11y-superseded.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-24-a11y-superseded.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 982, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:47\", \"token_count\": 310, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-01\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Core Engine Kickoff\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nKickoff for the core redaction engine. Charlie owns the first detect-and-mask pass on text-layer PDFs; Diana reviews the first commit. API and packaging stay out of scope for now.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-01\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Core Engine Kickoff\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're kicking off the core redaction engine today. This is the foundation for the rest of the toolkit, so I want a clear owner and a first deliverable. Charlie, can you take the initial implementation?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Yes. I'll start with a basic detect-and-mask path on text-layer PDFs. Nothing fancy yet — just enough to prove the engine can find spans and apply masks.\\n\\n**Bob**: Do you need anything from the API side for this first pass?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Not yet. Keep the API work separate until there's something stable to call into. If that changes I'll ping you.\\n\\n**Diana**: Once there's a first commit, I'll pick up review. Don't wait on a full test suite for that initial push.\\n\\n**Evan**: Same from packaging — no Docker or release concerns until the engine exists.\\n\\n**Alice**: Sounds good. Charlie, go ahead and open the task on your side; Diana reviews when there's something to look at. We'll expand from there.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Will do.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 01 firefli transcript core engin kickoff date 2026 06 01 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari kickoff for the core redact engin charli own the first detect and mask pas on text layer pdfs diana review the first commit api and packag stay out of scope for now sourc id src meet 01 firefli transcript core engin kickoff date 2026 06 01 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re kick off the core redact engin today this is the foundat for the rest of the toolkit so i want a clear owner and a first deliver charli can you take the initi implement charli yes i ll start with a basic detect and mask path on text layer pdfs noth fanci yet just enough to prove the engin can find span and appli mask bob do you need anyth from the api side for this first pas charli not yet keep the api work separ until there s someth stabl to call into if that chang i ll ping you diana onc there s a first commit i ll pick up review don t wait on a full test suit for that initi push evan same from packag no docker or releas concern until the engin exist alic sound good charli go ahead and open the task on your side diana review when there s someth to look at we ll expand from there charli will do\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94d220c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"id\": \"f9d456f461c99682\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23706519814598945, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05738105449427066, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6563282, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94d220c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1347, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:07\", \"token_count\": 395, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie opened on the AGPL PDF-parser problem and the search for an Apache/MIT alternative. Evan noted the earlier Windows path fix; code-signing cert procurement remains open.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: Licensing first — the replacement PDF parser Evan swapped in turned out to be AGPL. I've started searching for an Apache or MIT alternative. Need to confirm feature coverage before we swap again.\\n\\n**Diana**: Right — AGPL isn't acceptable for how we're distributing the toolkit.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Unknown how much rework another swap costs until I compare candidates. That's this week's task. I'd rather not guess.\\n\\n**Evan**: Separate note while we're all here — the Windows backslash path handling fix from earlier this month has been holding up fine in the build. No regressions there.\\n\\n**Alice**: Good to hear. And signing?\\n\\n**Evan**: Still waiting on the code-signing certificate to come through procurement. No firm timeline yet, so I can't say when that's cleared.\\n\\n**Alice**: Okay — Charlie, keep pushing on the parser alternative, that's the priority. Evan, keep chasing procurement on the cert, but no need for a deep-dive there today.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli open on the agpl pdf parser problem and the search for an apach mit altern evan note the earlier window path fix code sign cert procur remain open sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli licens first the replac pdf parser evan swap in turn out to be agpl i ve start search for an apach or mit altern need to confirm featur coverag befor we swap again diana right agpl isn t accept for how we re distribut the toolkit charli unknown how much rework anoth swap cost until i compar candid that s this week s task i d rather not guess evan separ note while we re all here the window backslash path handl fix from earlier this month ha been hold up fine in the build no regress there alic good to hear and sign evan still wait on the code sign certif to come through procur no firm timelin yet so i can t say when that s clear alic okay charli keep push on the parser altern that s the prioriti evan keep chase procur on the cert but no need for a deep dive there today\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e951fd048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"5bd1df00b489f9f3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23699084914598945, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05738105449427066, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65608037, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e951fd048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1335, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:03\", \"token_count\": 372, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-05\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Performance Benchmarks Blocker\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nEvan opened with the bare-metal blocker: scripts are ready, but the dedicated node still isn't provisioned. The team rejected shared/virtualized boxes as publishable evidence.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-05\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Performance Benchmarks Blocker\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-09\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Evan**: Quick update on bare-metal benchmarks — scripts are ready and tested locally, but I still don't have the dedicated node provisioned. I've chased it twice this week already.\\n\\n**Bob**: Could we run against one of the shared dev boxes in the meantime, just to get a rough number?\\n\\n**Evan**: I'd rather not — those boxes are virtualized and shared with other teams, so any noisy-neighbor load would throw off the numbers we'd be publishing.\\n\\n**Diana**: Agreed. If we publish something based on a shared box, we can't stand behind it if someone challenges the release claims later.\\n\\n**Alice**: Keep chasing the real hardware then. Let's not publish anything until we have it.\\n\\n**Bob**: Fine by me. Shared-box numbers aren't worth the argument later.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 05 firefli transcript perform benchmark blocker date 2026 08 09 particip alic pm bob backend diana qa evan devop summari evan open with the bare metal blocker script are readi but the dedic node still isn t provis the team reject share virtual box a publish evid sourc id src meet 05 firefli transcript perform benchmark blocker date 2026 08 09 particip alic pm bob backend diana qa evan devop transcript evan quick updat on bare metal benchmark script are readi and test local but i still don t have the dedic node provis i ve chase it twice this week alreadi bob could we run against one of the share dev box in the meantim just to get a rough number evan i d rather not those box are virtual and share with other team so ani noisi neighbor load would throw off the number we d be publish diana agre if we publish someth base on a share box we can t stand behind it if someon challeng the releas claim later alic keep chase the real hardwar then let s not publish anyth until we have it bob fine by me share box number aren t worth the argument later\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9429f808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-09-Performance-Benchmarks-Blocker.md\", \"id\": \"a8f6aa03aeb91f14\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23629663714598942, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05738105449427066, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65376633, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-09-Performance-Benchmarks-Blocker.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9429f808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-09-Performance-Benchmarks-Blocker.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-09-Performance-Benchmarks-Blocker.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1137, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:16\", \"token_count\": 339, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBob reported offline-auth rotation cannot complete without network access — left blocked. Evan's disk-usage monitor loop is in; Diana's halt-behavior sign-off still pending.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Bob**: Offline-auth mock first — not well. I built the local mock and ran the rotation flow with the network denied. Rotation can't complete offline.\\n\\n**Diana**: Is that a bug in the mock, or the design?\\n\\n**Bob**: The design. The flow we picked assumes a connection to finish rotation. I don't have a fix yet — we should call it blocked.\\n\\n**Alice**: Agreed. Offline auth stays blocked until we have an offline-capable rotation approach. Evan, status on the disk-usage monitor?\\n\\n**Evan**: Monitor loop is in. It watches disk usage so we can enforce the quota policy. Haven't had Diana sign off on the halt behavior yet.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Has anyone verified the halt behavior yet?\\n\\n**Evan**: Not signed off. Monitor is in progress; Diana still needs to confirm it actually stops writes at the configured quota.\\n\\n**Evan**: I'll wait on Diana's halt sign-off before calling quota monitoring done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari bob report offlin auth rotat can not complet without network access left block evan s disk usag monitor loop is in diana s halt behavior sign off still pend sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript bob offlin auth mock first not well i built the local mock and ran the rotat flow with the network deni rotat can t complet offlin diana is that a bug in the mock or the design bob the design the flow we pick assum a connect to finish rotat i don t have a fix yet we should call it block alic agre offlin auth stay block until we have an offlin capabl rotat approach evan status on the disk usag monitor evan monitor loop is in it watch disk usag so we can enforc the quota polici haven t had diana sign off on the halt behavior yet charli ha anyon verifi the halt behavior yet evan not sign off monitor is in progress diana still need to confirm it actual stop write at the configur quota evan i ll wait on diana s halt sign off befor call quota monitor done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"0d85de036037cfcd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23416535614598946, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05738105449427066, \"vector_similarity\": 0.64666206, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1273, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:13\", \"token_count\": 368, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMake the redaction suite compatible with Windows, including build packaging. A Windows build artifact now exists, but Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; the task remains active pending that certificate.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Windows build artifact is produced successfully.\\n\\n- Build is code-signed with a valid certificate so it is not blocked by Defender/SmartScreen.\\n\\n- Signed build passes Windows Defender/SmartScreen without warnings.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMake the redaction suite compatible with Windows, including build packaging. A Windows build artifact now exists, but Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; the task remains active pending that certificate.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-08**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because Windows OS compatibility is required for the release gate.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-02**: Evan - Signing Cert Missing (Active)\\n\\n - *Found that Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; task remains active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript make the redact suit compat with window includ build packag a window build artifact now exist but window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss the task remain activ pend that certif clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 accept criterion window build artifact is produc success build is code sign with a valid certif so it is not block by defend smartscreen sign build pass window defend smartscreen without warn clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript make the redact suit compat with window includ build packag a window build artifact now exist but window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss the task remain activ pend that certif clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 activ histori 2026 08 08 alic task creat open open the task becaus window o compat is requir for the releas gate 2026 09 02 evan sign cert miss activ found that window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss task remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e95e78f48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"id\": \"b781255db8f4d9fe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23342841814598947, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05738105449427066, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6442056, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e95e78f48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1115, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:51\", \"token_count\": 532, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e99eb05e8a