**: Fixed! Returning 404 now for empty states. :thumbsup:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 46 slack thread redact profil export api channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 14 2026 08 14 09 23 bob hey engin just push the initi implement for the export api you can hit v1 export profil on the dev branch now it should return the full pydant valid polici bundl 2026 08 14 09 28 charli nice doe it includ the regex manifest or is that a separ call i need to know what pattern were activ for the audit trail 2026 08 14 09 46 bob it s all in the one bundl i ve got a regex _ manifest key that map the pattern id to the actual compil string and their intern tag 2026 08 14 09 57 alic bob will this export includ the user defin overrid too we had that discuss in the standup about make sure manual review can see whi a rule wa bypass 2026 08 14 09 59 bob yeah the overrid list is includ it s basic a json dump of the current state of the profil 2026 08 14 10 36 diana just pull the latest and tri hit it with an uniniti profil it s return a 500 right now instead of a 404 i ll open a sub task but bob can you look at the null check on the profil _ manag 2026 08 14 10 39 bob my bad i see it the session wasn t be valid befor the export call push a fix to featur export api in 5 min pinch _ finger 2026 08 14 10 41 diana fix return 404 now for empti state thumbsup\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8dd842e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"id\": \"a0344269eb33520d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.47832083184156526, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.40003464548795037, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6609886, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8dd842e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1509, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:39\", \"token_count\": 445, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-08\\n\\n# Slack Thread: API Authentication Deferral\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:07] Bob**: Looking into REST API auth for v1.0. Do we need a full auth story now, or is trusted local network enough for the first release?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:22] Diana**: Given the PII involved, something robust would be nice. But if this is strictly local-network-only, we might not need it for v1.0.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 14:00] Bob**: Doing a short study either way — what we'd need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we rememb them rest auth with rotat support sinc v1 0 is local network onli 2026 08 0511 06 diana agre fold that into the defer work note so it surviv until v1 1 plan 2026 08 20 10 11 alic recheck releas scope for v1 0 auth stay defer to post v1 0 0 trust network assumpt still hold\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"id\": \"8320be9e419ec3ba\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36276943284757457, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.23334323263939233, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6647639, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1525, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 479, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-09\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Security Patch - CORS Issue\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-07-10\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:20] Diana**: @Bob, I just ran a security scan on the API. We've got a wide-open CORS policy. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is a no-go for this project.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:23] Bob**: Oops, that was left over from local testing on the scaffold. I'll tighten it up now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:43] Bob**: Applying the CORS patch. It now only allows requests from the defined `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in the environment config.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:50] Diana**: Scan is coming back clean now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:52] Bob**: Thanks for the catch, Diana. I've added a lint check to prevent `*` from being committed in the future.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 15:45] Alice**: Good catch. Let's make sure we don't have any other dev-only flags leaking into the main branch.\\n\\n**[2026-07-15 09:54] Diana**: Re-ran the CVE and CORS scans ahead of the release evidence pack — patch is still holding, no regressions since Bob's fix.\\n\\n**[2026-07-15 09:55] Bob**: Good. I'll note that in the security patch record.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 09 slack thread secur patch cor issu channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 07 10 last activ 2026 07 15 2026 07 10 14 20 diana bob i just ran a secur scan on the api we ve got a wide open cor polici access control allow origin is a no go for this project 2026 07 10 14 23 bob oop that wa left over from local test on the scaffold i ll tighten it up now 2026 07 10 14 43 bob appli the cor patch it now onli allow request from the defin allow _ origin in the environ config 2026 07 10 14 50 diana scan is come back clean now 2026 07 10 14 52 bob thank for the catch diana i ve ad a lint check to prevent from be commit in the futur 2026 07 1015 45 alic good catch let s make sure we don t have ani other dev onli flag leak into the main branch 2026 07 15 09 54 diana re ran the cve and cor scan ahead of the releas evid pack patch is still hold no regress sinc bob s fix 2026 07 15 09 55 bob good i ll note that in the secur patch record\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92a731a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"id\": \"19b85fe455718c06\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3362387724927628, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20002969641823257, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65405995, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92a731a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-07-10-security-patch.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1152, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:35\", \"token_count\": 369, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-21\\n\\n# Slack Thread: AES-256 Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:20] Bob**: Moving forward with the AES-256 pipeline now that the crypto eval settled on it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:28] Bob**: Merged it — every temp file in the processing queue is now encrypted with a per-session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:37] Diana**: Running a stress test. What happens if the system loses power mid-redaction? Does the encrypted temp file persist?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:38] Bob**: Yes, but it's useless without the session key, which only lives in volatile memory. On reboot, the cleanup hook wipes it anyway.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:39] Diana**: Makes sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:23] Diana**: Crypto sign-off done. Verified the `/tmp/cipherdoc` data is unreadable without the session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:41] Diana**: This also builds on the fail-closed work — the pipeline integrates with that deletion behavior cleanly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:43] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:44] Alice**: Nice. :white_check_mark:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 21 slack thread ae 256 encrypt pipelin channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 05 last activ 2026 08 07 2026 08 05 09 20 bob move forward with the ae 256 pipelin now that the crypto eval settl on it 2026 08 05 09 28 bob merg it everi temp file in the process queue is now encrypt with a per session key 2026 08 05 09 37 diana run a stress test what happen if the system lose power mid redact doe the encrypt temp file persist 2026 08 05 09 38 bob yes but it s useless without the session key which onli life in volatil memori on reboot the cleanup hook wipe it anyway 2026 08 05 09 39 diana make sens 2026 08 07 13 23 diana crypto sign off done verifi the tmp cipherdoc data is unread without the session key 2026 08 07 13 41 diana this also build on the fail close work the pipelin integr with that delet behavior clean 2026 08 07 13 43 bob call this done 2026 08 07 13 44 alic nice white _ check _ mark\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8df32f68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"id\": \"02d97ea3a8ab863b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3352757694927628, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20002969641823257, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65084994, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8df32f68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-05-aes256-pipeline.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1112, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:37\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-49\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 09:00] Charlie**: Switching to `tracemalloc` for the leak hunt since the usual profiler is a no-go on the offline lab box. Kicking off a fresh capture now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:05] Charlie**: Already got something. The `tracemalloc` output shows we're holding onto the full page-tree in `RedactionEngine` even after the document object is closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:50] Bob**: That lines up with the hotspot list from earlier this week. I'll start on a patch tonight.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:45] Bob**: Patch is in. Added explicit cleanup so the context manager actually releases the page-tree reference instead of just closing the file handle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:47] Diana**: Just finished a 6-hour soak test with the new build. Memory usage is flat as a pancake after the initial load. :pancake:\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:41] Alice**: Huge relief. Is this on top of the buffer-release fix from the large-file chunking rework, or a separate code path?\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:43] Bob**: Same family of fix — builds on the chunking buffer-release work. PR #84 is merged.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:44] Evan**: On it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:46] Evan**: Rolling this out to the dev clusters. @Charlie thanks for the tracemalloc deep dive.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 49 slack thread memori leak tracemalloc patch channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 21 last activ 2026 08 23 2026 08 21 09 00 charli switch to tracemalloc for the leak hunt sinc the usual profil is a no go on the offlin lab box kick off a fresh captur now 2026 08 21 11 05 charli alreadi got someth the tracemalloc output show we re hold onto the full page tree in redactionengin even after the document object is close 2026 08 21 11 50 bob that line up with the hotspot list from earlier this week i ll start on a patch tonight 2026 08 23 09 45 bob patch is in ad explicit cleanup so the context manag actual releas the page tree refer instead of just close the file handl 2026 08 23 09 47 diana just finish a 6 hour soak test with the new build memori usag is flat a a pancak after the initi load pancak 2026 08 23 10 41 alic huge relief is this on top of the buffer releas fix from the larg file chunk rework or a separ code path 2026 08 23 10 43 bob same famili of fix build on the chunk buffer releas work pr 84 is merg 2026 08 23 10 44 evan on it 2026 08 23 10 46 evan roll this out to the dev cluster charli thank for the tracemalloc deep dive\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"id\": \"824fb66730068003\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3284028054927628, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20002969641823257, \"vector_similarity\": 0.62794006, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1379, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:34\", \"token_count\": 428, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-05\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offset Mismatch Debugging\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 08:56] Charlie**: @Diana, I'm seeing weird behavior in the test cases. The redaction masks are shifted by a character or two in some PDF exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:01] Diana**: Multi-column layouts? I told you pdfminer output was injecting spaces.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:43] Charlie**: It's not just the spaces. The engine sees the text at one offset, but the PDF coordinates are different after the cleaning phase.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:51] Diana**: Are you seeing this on all viewers? Sometimes Acrobat renders overlays differently than Chrome's PDF viewer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:52] Charlie**: Looking at the raw coordinate output for now. Whitespace normalization looks like the culprit — non-breaking spaces keep showing up in the extracted text.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:53] Charlie**: Still stuck. Tried mapping cleaned offsets back to raw ones, but the math falls apart on dense pages.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:40] Diana**: Can we get most of the standard text aligned and park the edge cases?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:42] Charlie**: Not really — on dense docs it's closer to half the spans. Starting to look like an upstream pdfminer.six issue. I'm going to check their tracker.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:45] Alice**: Status?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:47] Charlie**: No. Offline tonight.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 05 slack thread offset mismatch debug channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 23 2026 06 23 08 56 charli diana i m see weird behavior in the test case the redact mask are shift by a charact or two in some pdf export 2026 06 23 09 01 diana multi column layout i told you pdfminer output wa inject space 2026 06 23 09 43 charli it s not just the space the engin see the text at one offset but the pdf coordin are differ after the clean phase 2026 06 23 10 51 diana are you see this on all viewer sometim acrobat render overlay differ than chrome s pdf viewer 2026 06 23 10 52 charli look at the raw coordin output for now whitespac normal look like the culprit non break space keep show up in the extract text 2026 06 23 10 53 charli still stuck tri map clean offset back to raw one but the math fall apart on dens page 2026 06 23 12 40 diana can we get most of the standard text align and park the edg case 2026 06 23 12 42 charli not realli on dens doc it s closer to half the span start to look like an upstream pdfminer six issu i m go to check their tracker 2026 06 23 12 45 alic status 2026 06 23 12 47 charli no offlin tonight\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e938a76e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"id\": \"feb7b0bf42cb1a60\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3273814974927628, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20002969641823257, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6245357, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e938a76e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1387, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:24\", \"token_count\": 405, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-07\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Blocked on Upstream PDF Library\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-26\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:10] Charlie**: Bad news on the offset mismatch fix. It's definitely coming from `pdfminer.six`. There's an open issue on their repo for the whitespace handling we're hitting.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:57] Alice**: Any workaround? We can't stay blocked on this forever.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:58] Charlie**: Leaving it blocked for now. Local patches aren't getting us a clean fix — it's too deep in the parser.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 14:18] Charlie**: Still watching upstream — there's a PR against pdfminer.six, #992, that should cover the whitespace fix, but it hasn't merged. No movement from the maintainers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 15:58] Charlie**: Spent some time this week evaluating whether we fork pdfminer.six ourselves to get the fix in sooner.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 16:01] Alice**: What's the team's read on that?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 17:55] Charlie**: We're passing on it. Maintaining a PDF parsing fork long-term is more risk than the wait. Staying blocked on #992.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:24] Charlie**: Checked again — #992 is still unmerged. No safe local path that doesn't involve owning a fork, so we're leaving the offset fix blocked pending the upstream merge.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Alice**: This is becoming a real risk for the v1.0 timeline.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Charlie**: Agreed, but I'd rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can't maintain.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 07 slack thread block on upstream pdf librari channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 26 last activ 2026 09 10 2026 06 26 09 10 charli bad news on the offset mismatch fix it s definit come from pdfminer six there s an open issu on their repo for the whitespac handl we re hit 2026 06 26 09 57 alic ani workaround we can t stay block on this forev 2026 06 26 09 58 charli leav it block for now local patch aren t get u a clean fix it s too deep in the parser 2026 08 05 14 18 charli still watch upstream there s a pr against pdfminer six 992 that should cover the whitespac fix but it hasn t merg no movement from the maintain 2026 08 20 15 58 charli spent some time this week evalu whether we fork pdfminer six ourselv to get the fix in sooner 2026 08 2016 01 alic what s the team s read on that 2026 08 2017 55 charli we re pass on it maintain a pdf pars fork long term is more risk than the wait stay block on 992 2026 09 1010 24 charli check again 992 is still unmerg no safe local path that doesn t involv own a fork so we re leav the offset fix block pend the upstream merg 2026 09 1010 41 alic this is becom a real risk for the v1 0 timelin 2026 09 1010 55 charli agre but i d rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can t maintain\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"id\": \"68389a2a4ecca69d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3099382172499784, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16666666749996908, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6442385, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1522, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:33\", \"token_count\": 462, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2980730898951665, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13335313127880932, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68241966, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-09\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n**Participants**: Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana reported the Electron-plus-CLI packaging test passed; desktop pack accepted.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-09\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n**Participants**: Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Packaging test for the desktop wrapper — clean. Electron shell plus the CLI path installed and ran on the test machines. I'm calling it a pass.\\n\\n**Evan**: Scaffold and installer path held up. IPC to the batch CLI is what made the GUI usable — without that it