uth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1525, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 479, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-38\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Build Artifact\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:05] Evan**: Path fix unblocked the Windows packaging attempt — I've got a build artifact out the other end now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:06] Bob**: Does it actually run, or just build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:24] Evan**: Runs. Installed it on a Windows box and it's passing the same sanity checks we run on Linux.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:26] Diana**: Does this mean Windows compatibility is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:36] Evan**: The engineering work for the Windows build is complete — packaging works, the binary is sound. Code-signing is a separate item we haven't even started on yet, so I wouldn't call the whole thing closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:45] Alice**: Understood, we'll track signing on its own. Good progress on the build itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 38 slack thread window build artifact channel releas date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 05 evan path fix unblock the window packag attempt i ve got a build artifact out the other end now 2026 08 12 09 06 bob doe it actual run or just build 2026 08 12 09 24 evan run instal it on a window box and it s pass the same saniti check we run on linux 2026 08 12 09 26 diana doe this mean window compat is done 2026 08 12 09 36 evan the engin work for the window build is complet packag work the binari is sound code sign is a separ item we haven t even start on yet so i wouldn t call the whole thing close 2026 08 12 09 45 alic understood we ll track sign on it own good progress on the build itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"id\": \"61bccaf0a0dfface\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2514470218327593, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07238241404679903, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66926444, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 859, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:30\", \"token_count\": 268, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-01\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Core Engine Kickoff\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nKickoff for the core redaction engine. Charlie owns the first detect-and-mask pass on text-layer PDFs; Diana reviews the first commit. API and packaging stay out of scope for now.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-01\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Core Engine Kickoff\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're kicking off the core redaction engine today. This is the foundation for the rest of the toolkit, so I want a clear owner and a first deliverable. Charlie, can you take the initial implementation?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Yes. I'll start with a basic detect-and-mask path on text-layer PDFs. Nothing fancy yet — just enough to prove the engine can find spans and apply masks.\\n\\n**Bob**: Do you need anything from the API side for this first pass?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Not yet. Keep the API work separate until there's something stable to call into. If that changes I'll ping you.\\n\\n**Diana**: Once there's a first commit, I'll pick up review. Don't wait on a full test suite for that initial push.\\n\\n**Evan**: Same from packaging — no Docker or release concerns until the engine exists.\\n\\n**Alice**: Sounds good. Charlie, go ahead and open the task on your side; Diana reviews when there's something to look at. We'll expand from there.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Will do.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 01 firefli transcript core engin kickoff date 2026 06 01 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari kickoff for the core redact engin charli own the first detect and mask pas on text layer pdfs diana review the first commit api and packag stay out of scope for now sourc id src meet 01 firefli transcript core engin kickoff date 2026 06 01 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re kick off the core redact engin today this is the foundat for the rest of the toolkit so i want a clear owner and a first deliver charli can you take the initi implement charli yes i ll start with a basic detect and mask path on text layer pdfs noth fanci yet just enough to prove the engin can find span and appli mask bob do you need anyth from the api side for this first pas charli not yet keep the api work separ until there s someth stabl to call into if that chang i ll ping you diana onc there s a first commit i ll pick up review don t wait on a full test suit for that initi push evan same from packag no docker or releas concern until the engin exist alic sound good charli go ahead and open the task on your side diana review when there s someth to look at we ll expand from there charli will do\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94d220c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"id\": \"f9d456f461c99682\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24266874934480748, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06593379906401074, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6550503, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94d220c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-06-01-Core-Engine-Kickoff.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1347, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:07\", \"token_count\": 395, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-37\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Signing Gap\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 09:14] Evan**: Windows Defender and SmartScreen are both flagging the build for pilot testers — unsigned binaries get treated as untrusted by default.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:13] Alice**: Is the missing code-signing certificate the actual blocker here?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:14] Evan**: Yes. We still don't have one. Until we do, every pilot install is going to trip a warning at best, get blocked outright at worst.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:16] Diana**: Release blocker?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23851345078567301, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05935357969381859, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65655315, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signi